<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Use Case Specification - UC-17</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 40px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    font-size: 11pt;
  }
  h2 {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  td {
    border: 1px solid #000000;
    padding: 8px 12px;
    vertical-align: top;
    font-size: 10pt;
  }
  .label-cell {
    font-weight: bold;
    width: 20%;
    background-color: #F3F4F6;
  }
  .header-title {
    background-color: #E5E7EB;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 14pt;
    padding: 10px;
  }
  .flow-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .flow-list li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .sub-list {
    margin-top: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    list-style-type: lower-alpha;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <h2>Use Case Specification</h2>

  <table>
    <tbody>
      <!-- Title Row -->
      <tr>
        <td colspan="4" class="header-title">UC-17: Manage Team Invitations</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Created Info -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Created By:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">Nguyen Khoi Nguyen</td>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Date Created:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">2026-06-17</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Actors -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell">Primary Actor:</td>
        <td>Participant (Thí sinh)</td>
        <td class="label-cell">Secondary Actors:</td>
        <td>None</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Trigger -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Trigger:</td>
        <td colspan="3">A Team Leader decides to invite a member to their team, or a Participant wants to respond to a pending invitation they received.</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Description -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Description:</td>
        <td colspan="3">The "Manage Team Invitations" use case describes the process by which a Team Leader sends an invitation to other participants to join their team, and how the invited participants can accept or reject the invitation. It also covers the Leader's ability to revoke a sent invitation.</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Preconditions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Preconditions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>PRE-1:</b> The user is logged in as a Participant.</li>
            <li><b>PRE-2:</b> The team is already created (for the Team Leader) and the team has not reached the maximum member limit.</li>
            <li><b>PRE-3:</b> The invited participant is registered in the same Hackathon and is currently not a member of any team.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Post-conditions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Post-conditions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>POST-1:</b> If accepted, the invited participant is added to the team roster, and the invitation status changes to "Accepted".</li>
            <li><b>POST-2:</b> If rejected, the invitation status changes to "Rejected".</li>
            <li><b>POST-3:</b> If revoked, the invitation is either set to "Revoked" or removed from the database.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Normal Flow -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Normal Flow:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ol class="flow-list">
            <li>The Team Leader logs into the dashboard and navigates to the "My Team" panel.</li>
            <li>The Team Leader enters the email address or username of the participant they want to invite.</li>
            <li>The Team Leader clicks the "Send Invitation" button.</li>
            <li>The system validates that the target user exists, is registered in the hackathon, is not currently in a team, and has no pending invitation from this team <b>[see 1-EF, 2-EF]</b>.</li>
            <li>The system creates a pending invitation record in the database and sends a notification to the invited participant <b>[see 2-AF, 3-EF]</b>.</li>
            <li>The invited participant logs in, navigates to the "My Invitations" section, and sees the pending invite.</li>
            <li>The invited participant clicks the "Accept" button <b>[see 1-AF]</b>.</li>
            <li>The system verifies that the team still has open slots and the participant has not joined another team <b>[see 2-EF, 4-EF]</b>.</li>
            <li>The system adds the participant to the team database, updates the invitation status to "Accepted", and sends a success notification to the Team Leader.</li>
          </ol>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Alternative Flows -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Alternative Flows:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0;"><b>1-AF: Rejecting the invitation</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>a. In Step 7 of the Normal Flow, the invited participant clicks the "Reject" button.</li>
            <li>b. The system updates the invitation status to "Rejected" in the database.</li>
            <li>c. The system sends a notification to the Team Leader indicating the invitation was declined.</li>
            <li>d. The use case ends.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p style="margin:8px 0 6px 0;"><b>2-AF: Revoking a sent invitation</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>a. After Step 5 of the Normal Flow, the Team Leader navigates to the "Sent Invitations" list.</li>
            <li>b. The Team Leader clicks "Revoke" next to the pending invitation.</li>
            <li>c. The system updates the status of the invitation to "Revoked" (or deletes it) in the database.</li>
            <li>d. The system notifies the invited participant that the invitation has been withdrawn.</li>
            <li>e. The use case ends.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Exceptions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Exceptions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <p style="margin:0 0 6px 0;"><b>1-EF: Target user already in a team or already invited</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>1. In Step 4, the system detects that the target user is already in a team or has a pending invitation from this team.</li>
            <li>2. The system displays an error message: "User is already a member of a team or has a pending invitation."</li>
            <li>3. The use case terminates.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p style="margin:8px 0 6px 0;"><b>2-EF: Maximum team size reached</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>1. In Step 4 or 8, the system detects that adding this member would exceed the maximum team size limit defined for the hackathon.</li>
            <li>2. The system displays an error message: "Cannot invite/accept. The team is full."</li>
            <li>3. The use case terminates.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p style="margin:8px 0 6px 0;"><b>3-EF: Database write failure</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>1. In Step 5, the system fails to create the invitation record due to a database connection error.</li>
            <li>2. The system displays an error message: "Action failed due to a database error."</li>
            <li>3. The use case terminates.</li>
          </ul>
          
          <p style="margin:8px 0 6px 0;"><b>4-EF: Participant already joined another team</b></p>
          <ul class="flow-list" style="list-style-type:none; padding-left:10px;">
            <li>1. In Step 8, the system detects that the participant has accepted another team's invite in the meantime.</li>
            <li>2. The system displays an error message: "Invitation is no longer valid as the user has joined another team."</li>
            <li>3. The use case terminates.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Priority & Frequency -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Priority:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">High</td>
        <td class="label-cell" style="width:15%;">Frequency of Use:</td>
        <td style="width:35%;">High (Used heavily during the team formation phase of a hackathon)</td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Business Rules -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Business Rules:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li><b>BR-1: Maximum Team Size:</b> The number of members in a team cannot exceed the maximum team size set by the organizer for the hackathon (e.g., 5 members).</li>
            <li><b>BR-2: Single Team Rule:</b> A participant can only be an active member of one team per hackathon event.</li>
            <li><b>BR-3: Role Authorization:</b> Only the Team Leader (creator of the team) is authorized to send or revoke team invitations.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Other Information -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Other Information:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          None.
        </td>
      </tr>
      
      <!-- Assumptions -->
      <tr>
        <td class="label-cell" colspan="1">Assumptions:</td>
        <td colspan="3">
          <ul class="flow-list">
            <li>Participants are registered in the hackathon before receiving invites.</li>
            <li>Email or system notifications are operational and reliable.</li>
          </ul>
        </td>
      </tr>
      
    </tbody>
  </table>

</body>
</html>
